NAME
       readlink - read the target of a symbolic link

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       ssize_t readlink(const char *path, char *buf, size_t size);

DESCRIPTION
       Places the target of the symbolic link at PATH into BUF without
       following it. The result is not terminated, so terminate it at
       the returned length yourself.

       A return equal to SIZE means the target may have been truncated;
       retry with a larger buffer.

RETURN VALUE
       The number of bytes placed in BUF, or -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EINVAL   the path is not a symbolic link
       ENOENT   the path does not exist

SEE ALSO
       symlink(2), stat(2), ln(1)
